# __PROJECT_NAME__

Bootstrapped from `project-template`. Read these before doing anything stack-specific:

- **`docs/project-profile.md`** — the stack contract: platform, targeted/component/phase validation tiers, test frameworks, UI/E2E harness, shared-resource locks, project layout, run instructions, git workflow, human tasks, budgets. Agents trust this file over their own assumptions.
- **`.github/instructions/copilot.instructions.md`** — coding standards (per-stack sections; the profile says which applies).
- **`supporting-files/AGENT_FLOWS.md`** — how the agent pipeline fits together.

House rules:

- Agent definitions (`.codex/agents/*.toml`, `.claude/agents/`, `.github/agents/`) and skills (`.agents/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`) are **generated** from `agents-src/` / `skills-src/` and kept current by the weekly template-sync PR. Change them in `project-template` and let the sync bring them here — local edits to synced files are overwritten by the next sync. CI (`agents-drift-check`) fails on drift between source and rendered files.
- No agent pins a model — everything inherits the session model.
- All agents communicate via the structured Agent Report format defined in their definitions.
- `main` is protected; follow the git workflow contract in the project profile.
- Every skill run has a persistent Steward (on Codex the coordinator executes its duties). Answer a Steward Challenge in your next report before your next gate; a Steward Hold blocks that gate until the coordinator clears it. Keep `docs/project-profile.md` § Delivery posture current so its scrutiny stays proportionate.

Codex specifics:

- Trust this repo on your first `codex` run — `.codex/config.toml` (sandbox, approvals, MCP servers) and `.codex/agents/` only load in trusted projects.
- The delivery pipelines are the skills in `.agents/skills/`: `validate-with-waitlist`, `build-with-agent-team-light` (streamlined, one consolidated planning gate), and `build-with-agent-team` (expansive) — invoke via `/skills` or by asking for them.
- Subagent fan-out is capped by `[agents] max_threads` in `.codex/config.toml`; `/agent` switches between spawned agent threads.
